WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.200
Over the past generation, tremendous
productivity growth has allowed the US

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:13.860
dairy farms and processors to become
globally competitive. However, despite

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.970
this growth, outdated policies that are
counterproductive to the dairy economy

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:23.850
remain in place. Such policies include
the 80 year-old Orwellian "Federal Milk

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:28.230
Marketing Orders", a concoction of
convoluted US pricing regulations; the

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:33.300
selectively-protectionist import
barriers that suited the old inefficient

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:39.390
US milk industry; and lastly, the recent
subsidized margin insurance scheme, which

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.649
offers periodic payments designed to be
highly favorable to small, inefficient

00:00:43.649 --> 00:00:48.480
farms. This program may become costly,
harms lower-cost farms, and adds little

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.770
to risk management. These programs may benefit some farms and processors – often

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:56.309
the least productive – but do so at the
expense of taxpayers, consumers, and the

00:00:56.309 --> 00:01:00.920
broad dairy industry. It is now time to
let the US milk producers and processors

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:07.460
embrace their global competitiveness and
innovate unencumbered by obsolete policy approaches.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:12.500
What do you think about US
dairy subsidy schemes? Let us know in

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:16.560
your comments. Also, let us know what
other topics you'd like our scholars to

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:22.170
